    includes: ["Make sure you: the pass-critical must-hits, translated from thresholds + agents", "Do: on-brand guidance", "Don't: the avoids"],
    worked: `<p><b>Make sure you</b></p><ul><li>Hook us in the first couple of seconds, open on the oil lifting off the stone.</li><li>Keep the Volcanic Roller on screen for most of the video.</li><li>Show yourself actually using it, rolling it across your skin.</li><li>Say Luna Roca at least twice.</li><li>Add captions on the key lines, so it works with the sound off.</li><li>Record somewhere quiet, clear sound.</li><li>End with a clear call to action, where to get it.</li></ul><p><b>Do</b></p><ul><li>Show real, everyday use.</li><li>Show the before and after clearly.</li><li>Keep it clean, authentic and high-energy.</li><li>Highlight the benefits: matte, portable, eco.</li></ul><p><b>Don't</b></p><ul><li>Shoot in poor lighting.</li><li>Overuse filters or use cluttered backgrounds.</li><li>Exaggerate or make false claims.</li><li>Create overly scripted or unnatural content.</li><li>Ignore the brand colors.</li></ul>`,
